{
  "headline": "Corn is at $4.51½ after four lower closes; hogs fell 4.1%",
  "lead": "Dec corn is at $4.51½ after four lower closes, with a fast harvest piling bushels on a market that was already heavy. A bounce of 2¾ cents does not change that.",
  "teaser": "Corn bounces after four lower closes, and December hogs settled 4.1% lower Tuesday.",
  "one_number": {
    "value": "4",
    "unit": "straight lower Dec corn closes",
    "context": "Dec corn settled lower four sessions running through Tuesday's $4.48¾. The overnight bounce to $4.51½ is only 2¾ cents of that slide."
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Grains bounce off lows",
      "body": "- Dec corn is at **$4.51½** overnight, up 0.6%, and Nov soybeans are at $12.36, up 6¾ cents.\n- Feedstuffs said a swift harvest sank corn and soy prices Tuesday, and AgWeb reported beans bounced early on China buying.\n- Wheat is at $6.13¼, up 3 cents after a lower close Tuesday.",
      "so_what": "Dry weather keeps combines moving and supply growing.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
      "overnight_surprise": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Hogs drop, cattle hold",
      "body": "- December hogs settled Tuesday at **$62.025**, down 4.1% from Monday's $64.675.\n- Feeder cattle settled at $352.80, up 0.8%, and October live cattle at $230.00 were unchanged.\n- Nothing in today's news explains the hog drop.",
      "so_what": "Hogs sit near the bottom of their 52-week range.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
      "overnight_surprise": true
    },
    {
      "title": "Crude climbs, gas gains",
      "body": "- WTI is at **$101.66** overnight, up 1.8% from Tuesday's $99.90 settle.\n- Oilprice.com reported renewed Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia reignited supply fears.\n- Natural gas is at $3.08, up 14.1% from a $2.70 settle, and nothing in the news explains that move.",
      "so_what": "Fuel for drying and hauling costs more than it did Tuesday.",
      "conviction_level": "medium",
      "overnight_surprise": true
    }
  ],
